M10_Chinook_ParaDrop: bound the owner-id parameter buffer.

M10_Chinook_ParaDrop::Created formatted its owner's object id into
char params[10] with sprintf. A dynamic id (>= 1500000000) has ten digits and
needs 11 bytes, so the write overflowed by one byte. The script is not bound
or attached in retail M10 data; the buffer is enlarged to 16 bytes and the
write bounded with snprintf for consistency with the M03 paradrop fix. The
formatted text is unchanged for every id.

--- a/Mission10.cpp
+++ b/Mission10.cpp
@@ -1768,8 +1768,8 @@
 
 		dead = false;
 		out = 0;
-		char params[10];
-		sprintf(params, "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
+		char params[16];
+		snprintf(params, sizeof(params), "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
 		Commands->Attach_Script(chinook, "M10_Reinforcement_Chinook", params);
 
 		chinook_id = Commands->Get_ID(chinook);
